{
  "_note": [
    "The state vocabulary of spec 014, as CASES rather than as prose. `api/domain/jobs.py` and",
    "`web/src/domain/jobs.ts` are both asserted against this file, so a word changed on one side alone",
    "fails one test that names the row. Same mechanism as `event-parity.json` (spec 010) and",
    "`scaffold-steps.json` (spec 013): one rule, two runtimes, one fixture.",
    "",
    "Every row is a payload the PLATFORM can send. The rows that matter most are the ones where a",
    "convenient field and an honest field disagree — `IDLE`+`FAILED` and `TERMINATED`+`FAILED` — because",
    "those are the rows a lazy implementation passes by accident and a screenshot catches."
  ],
